<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Waren (Müritz)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Waren is a town in Mecklenburg, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, on the northern shore of the Müritz, the largest lake lying wholly within Germany. Founded in the 13th century, it belonged to the lords of Werle, who had a residence there, and later to Mecklenburg. It is now the main town of the Müritz National Park region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/waren-muritz.jpg" alt="Waren (Müritz)" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: H.Helmlechner · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Stadthafen_Waren_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
